From: GapKeep <noreply@gapkeep.org>
Subject: dwhci: a short packet ends an IN data stage with split transactions

A low-speed device behind a high-speed hub is reached with split
transactions through the hub's transaction translator, one packet a
transaction. CDWHCITransferStageData::TransactionComplete() then counted
packets down to the end of the requested length, and never stopped at a
short packet, as the controller does by itself without splits. A device
that has sent all it has answers the next IN with NAK until the status
stage, so a request for more than the device returns timed out: on the
rig, a DigiMacro (V-USB) behind a Genesys hub answered GET_DESCRIPTOR for
the language IDs (wLength 255, 4 bytes sent) with NAK to every following
complete-split. Circle's own string reads ask for the exact length (4,
then bLength), so they never met it.

A zero-length IN packet is now counted as 0 bytes, not a whole packet
(the transfer size the controller leaves is right for IN; Linux dwc2
reads it the same way), so it ends the stage too.

--- a/lib/usb/dwhcixferstagedata.cpp
+++ b/lib/usb/dwhcixferstagedata.cpp
@@ -301,7 +301,8 @@
 	    && m_nBytesPerTransaction > 0)
 	{
 		if (   m_bSplitTransaction
-		    && m_bSplitComplete)
+		    && m_bSplitComplete
+		    && !m_bIn)		// gapkeep: an IN's count is right, 0 too (see below)
 		{
 			nBytesTransfered = m_nMaxPacketSize * nPacketsTransfered;
 		}
@@ -353,6 +354,22 @@
 
 	m_nPackets -= nPacketsTransfered;
 
+	// gapkeep: a short packet (or a zero-length one) ends an IN data stage.
+	// Without split transactions the controller sees to that; with them
+	// each packet is a transaction of its own, and the next one was asked
+	// for anyway. A device that has sent all it had answers that with NAK
+	// until the status stage, so a request for more than the device has
+	// (a string descriptor read with wLength 255, through a hub's
+	// transaction translator) timed out.
+	if (   m_bSplitTransaction
+	    && m_bSplitComplete
+	    && m_bIn
+	    && nPacketsTransfered > 0
+	    && nBytesTransfered < m_nMaxPacketSize)
+	{
+		m_nPackets = 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!m_bSplitTransaction)
 	{
 		if (!IsIsochronous ())
